              "start": 2
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Territory of Guam and the United States dispute liability for environmental hazards at the Ordot Dump, a site built by the Navy in the 1940s where both parties have allegedly deposited waste."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Court",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "9d333f89c250927d1987bbf1c9318ed8c17199d88cf09447fb6882bee30910fa",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-9d333f89c250-0001-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 12,
              "start": 12
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "The Court held that the natural reading of \u00a7\u202f113(f)(3)(B) limits a party\u2019s right to seek contribution under CERCLA to situations where the party has settled a CERCLA\u2011specific liability, and therefore reversed the Court of Appeals judgment and remanded for further proceedings."
      }
    ],
